-- title:
--   Theorem 1.10 — Liouville in rational rank 1, non-trivial Poisson boundary in rational rank at least 3
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finitely generated subgroup of $\mathrm{IET}$, with angle group $\Lambda(G)$.
--
--   1. If $\Lambda(G)$ has rational rank $1$, then every finitely supported, symmetric probability measure $\mu$ on $G$ is Liouville: every bounded $\mu$-harmonic function, $f(g) = \sum_h \mu(h) f(gh)$, on the semigroup generated by the support of $\mu$ is constant there.
--   2. If $\Lambda(G)$ has rational rank at least $3$, $G$ contains every rotation $x \mapsto x + a$ with $a \in \Lambda(G)$, and $G$ contains an element that is not such a rotation, then every finitely supported probability measure $\mu$ on $G$ whose support generates $G$ has non-trivial Poisson–Furstenberg boundary: some bounded $\mu$-harmonic function on $G$ is not constant.
--
--   Juschenko, Matte Bon, Monod and de la Salle, p. 5: “Theorem 1.10. Let $G < \mathrm{IET}$ be finitely generated. (i) If $\mathrm{rk}_{\mathbf Q}(G) = 1$ then every symmetric, finitely supported probability measure $\mu$ on $G$ has the Liouville property. (ii) Assume that $\mathrm{rk}_{\mathbf Q}(G) \ge 3$ and, viewing $\Lambda(G)$ as a subgroup of $\mathrm{IET}$ consisting of rotations, assume that $G$ contains $\Lambda(G)$ strictly. Then every finitely supported, non-degenerate probability measure on $G$ has non-trivial Poisson–Furstenberg boundary.” Non-degenerate is defined on p. 5: “its support generates the group”.
-- source:
--   Juschenko, K., Matte Bon, N., Monod, N. and de la Salle, M., Extensive amenability and an application to interval exchanges, Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems 38 (2018) 195–219, https://doi.org/10.1017/etds.2016.32 (arXiv:1503.04977v1, whose page numbers are used), p. 5, Theorem 1.10

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_IntervalExchange

open IntervalExchange

namespace JMMS

theorem isLiouville_of_rationalRank_eq_one_and_hasNontrivialBoundary_of_three_le_rationalRank
    (G : Subgroup (Equiv.Perm UnitAddCircle)) (hG : G ≤ IET) (hfg : G.FG) :
    (rationalRank (angleGroup G) = 1 →
      ∀ μ : ↥G →₀ ℝ, ThompsonAmenability.IsProbability μ → IsSymmetric μ →
        ThompsonAmenability.IsLiouville μ) ∧
    (3 ≤ rationalRank (angleGroup G) → (∀ a ∈ angleGroup G, rotation a ∈ G) →
      (∃ g ∈ G, ∀ a ∈ angleGroup G, g ≠ rotation a) →
      ∀ μ : ↥G →₀ ℝ, ThompsonAmenability.IsProbability μ → IsNondegenerate μ →
        HasNontrivialBoundary μ) := by
  sorry

end JMMS
